@InProceedings{boureau10cvpr,
  Title                    = {Learning mid-level features for recognition},
  Author                   = {Y.-L. Boureau and F. Bach and Y. LeCun and J. Ponce},
  Booktitle                = cvpr,
  Year                     = {2010},

  File                     = {boureau10cvpr.pdf:boureau10cvpr.pdf:PDF},
  Review                   = {Finds that max pooling is better than average pooling for both hard and soft assign BoW, besides for sparse coding. 

Max pooling over random instead of spatial pyramid regions also improves performance (far less than using the true SPM regions),
this is not true when average pooling is used. Average pooling over random patches is merely a (poorer) estimate from the BoW histogram than the complete image BoW histogram. The max over a smaller region is not an estimator of the max over the complete image.

Macro features concatenate a set of low-level descriptors, eg 2x2 sifts to yield a 2x2x128=512 d descriptor

Some theoretical analysis of why max-pooling could be leading to more discriminative description, not too convincing.}
}

