@InProceedings{hariharan12eccv,
  Title                    = {Discriminative Decorrelation for Clustering and Classification},
  Author                   = {B. Hariharan and J. Malik and D. Ramanan},
  Booktitle                = eccv,
  Year                     = {2012},

  File                     = {hariharan12eccv.pdf:hariharan12eccv.pdf:PDF},
  Review                   = {Fisher discriminant given by Sigma^{-1}(m_0 - m_1) generative learning of class conditional models with shared cov matrix, plugged into Bayes rule.

They argue that the mean of the negative class m_0 can be estimated class independent, since it is roughly the overall sample mean, if the possitive class is small.
However, we are interested in the difference of the class center vectors.

It turns out that (m_+ - m_- ) = (m_0 - m_+) *N / (N-M) where N is the overall number of samples and M is the nr of positive samples. Thus we show that we can get the difference vector exactly from the overall sample mean and count, together witht the positive sample mean and count.}
}

