  Author                   = {M. Nguyen and L. Torresani and F. de la Torre and C. Rother},
  Booktitle                = iccv,
  Year                     = {2009},

  File                     = {nguyen09iccv.pdf:nguyen09iccv.pdf:PDF},
  Owner                    = {verbeek},
  Review                   = {Detect objects from weak supervision for image classification, 
image score is given by score of max scoring subwindow

Multiple-instance learning framework:
o pos image should have at least one positively classified window
o neg image should have no postively classified windows.

Uses constraint generation to add most violated constraint in each step for negative images.
For positives, taking the max scoring at each step ensures that the max after parmeter change also satisfies constraint (maybe another max, but then also satisfies)
For negatives, taking max does not suffice, as it should be below threshold, and pushing the current max under threshold might leave another above threshold.

Uses ESS to search efficiently over subwindows.

Compared to SVM over BoW of complete image, and manual bounding boxes.
Outperforms both, as subwindow is more discriminative, and ground truth bounding box might exclude discriminative context.},
  Timestamp                = {2009.10.16}
}

