  Owner                    = {verbeek},
  Review                   = {The color descriptor used here can itself be interpreted as a Fisher Vector over a Gaussian on the RGB values in each of the 4 x 4 spatial bins of the patch.
There is no discounting effect here, and we could try it out by putting a prior on the Gaussian mean and variance, and computing gradients wrt hyperparameters.
This would double the patch descriptor to size (4 x 4) (spatial) x 3 (RGB) x 2 (mean + var) x 2 (hyper params per param) = 192 dim

What would happen if we would do the same thing on the gradient magnitudes in both x and y direction (eg no orientation binning) ?
In the same setup as above with non-iid Gaussian models we get a descriptor of (4 x 4) (spatial) x 2 (x and y) x 2 (mean + var) x 2 (hyper params per param) = 128 dim},
  Timestamp                = {2011.02.21}
}

